# Language reference docs

When adding or changing a **user-facing language feature**, update [`docs/language-reference/`](docs/language-reference/) in the same change.

## Layout

- One markdown file per feature under a section folder (`core/`, `types/`, `symbols/`, `environment/`, `modules/`, `tooling/`).
- Each section has a `README.md` index; the root has [`README.md`](docs/language-reference/README.md) and [`INDEX.md`](docs/language-reference/INDEX.md).

## Required updates

1. Edit or add the feature page (what / syntax / semantics / examples / **Related** links).
2. Link it from the section `README.md` and from [`INDEX.md`](docs/language-reference/INDEX.md).
3. Cross-link related pages (and from related pages back).
4. Point at `examples/*.thunk` when a good example exists.
5. Do not leave LANGUAGE/FEATURES as the only description of a new surface feature — reference pages are the browseable source of truth for “how does X work?”.

## Tone

Short, concrete, example-first. Prefer linking to design essays in `docs/LANGUAGE.md` for deep rationale instead of duplicating them.
